04 / HOW WE THINK
From a question
to a working concept.
Good research is more than collecting interesting facts. It requires careful questions, evidence, critical thinking, and the willingness to revise an idea when the evidence changes.

The research framework
A flexible process for investigating ideas and developing projects responsibly.

01
Define the question
Identify the problem, scope, assumptions, and what needs to be understood.
02
Study the evidence
Consult reliable sources, scientific literature, and established principles.
03
Develop the concept
Create a hypothesis, design, model, or simulation based on the evidence.
04
Evaluate and improve
Review results, document limitations, and identify what should happen next.
